  - title: A hundred thousand or fifty
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - The Kims have an old printer in the back room. Jae-hoon says we could do fifty copies. One for every house, and a few for the library.
    - Or a hundred thousand, everywhere, with brighter curtains and a tower on every page. Marcus says the money would mean he could leave his job.
    - I keep looking at the drawing of your farm. It's the only page they didn't want to change.
    - What would you do?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Print fifty copies
      replyA:
      - Fifty. One for every house. Cracks and weeds and all.
      - Jae-hoon says the printer makes a noise like a goose. I'm going to love that goose.
      flagsA:
      - street_book_printed
      optionB: Sign with the big publisher
      replyB:
      - A hundred thousand. Everywhere. For Marcus. For us.
      - I'll do the brighter curtains. I'll do the porch. I'll draw the tower very, very lightly.
      flagsB:
      - lena_sterling_book
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Fifty copies
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - The goose printer printed fifty. Some of the pages are a bit wonky. Walt says that's 'character'.
    - I gave them out yesterday, one on every doorstep. Emeka helped, of course. He said it was the best delivery of his life.
    - Gus read his page three times and then told me his window was drawn the wrong size. It isn't. He knows it isn't.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
